        "heading": "The UK's Gold Standard For Upholstery Safety",
        "body": "<p>UKFR is the United Kingdom Fire Resistance Standard, which means that every piece of furniture has to pass fire safety tests set by UK law.  This law ensures that materials like leather, fabric and foam don’t catch fire instantly. Moreover, it allows fire to burn slowly and allows people to evacuate the place if a fire event occurs.<br/><br/></p>"
